{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqpzvfu3u72","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","title":"Phase 1 code extractor handles CommonJS plus ESM and returns files symbols edges","summary":"The Phase-1 AST extractor (lib/code-extract/, extractRepo(repoPath,opts); CLI scripts/code-extract.js) is PURE extraction — no daemon/overlay/KB writes. It returns { repo, files:[{path,role}], symbols:[{name,kind,file,start_line,end_line,signature,exported,class?}], edges:[{from,to,kind 'calls'|'imports',external?}], stats }. kind is function|class|method|arrow. Non-obvious and load-bearing for the code-index sync phase: it parses BOTH CommonJS (require(), module.exports={...}, exports.foo=) and ESM (import/export), because this codebase is largely CJS — so the exported flag and import edges are correct for CJS modules (e.g. createWorktree/gateTask/compileSearchContext report exported=true via module.exports, even though they have no ESM export keyword). Call edges are per-FILE callee names (from=file, to=callee identifier; member calls like a.b.c() yield 'c'; require excluded). Symbol-to-symbol call resolution is intentionally deferred to a later phase. Import edges resolve local specifiers to repo-relative module paths (external true marks package/unresolved). Built on @babel/parser only (hand-rolled recursive descent, no @babel/traverse). Verified on own lib/: 95 files, 0 parse failures, 1048 symbols, 3199 edges.","category":"project","tags":["native-onboarder","code-index","ast","code-extract","phase1"],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-23T01:57:38.667Z","vec":[-0.1770651936531067,-0.01915932074189186,-0.04598009213805199,0.040757179260253906,0.0513543039560318,-0.05891876295208931,-0.051953498274087906,0.060281626880168915,-0.02214799076318741,-0.02385539561510086,0.014507146552205086,-0.0035971251782029867,-0.009044128470122814,-0.06168096512556076,0.03704220429062843,0.005418224260210991,-0.02135821431875229,0.009796332567930222,-0.013524864800274372,-0.06556026637554169,0.05706986