{"evt":"summary_set","id":"note:note-mqpzvfu3u72","workspace":"D:\\zonoid","summary":"The Phase-1 AST extractor (lib/code-extract/, extractRepo(repoPath,opts); CLI scripts/code-extract.js) is PURE extraction — no daemon/overlay/KB writes. It returns { repo, files:[{path,role}], symbols:[{name,kind,file,start_line,end_line,signature,exported,class?}], edges:[{from,to,kind 'calls'|'imports',external?}], stats }. kind is function|class|method|arrow. Non-obvious and load-bearing for the code-index sync phase: it parses BOTH CommonJS (require(), module.exports={...}, exports.foo=) and ESM (import/export), because this codebase is largely CJS — so the exported flag and import edges are correct for CJS modules (e.g. createWorktree/gateTask/compileSearchContext report exported=true via module.exports, even though they have no ESM export keyword). Call edges are per-FILE callee names (from=file, to=callee identifier; member calls like a.b.c() yield 'c'; require excluded). Symbol-to-symbol call resolution is intentionally deferred to a later phase. Import edges resolve local specifiers to repo-relative module paths (external true marks package/unresolved). Built on @babel/parser only (hand-rolled recursive descent, no @babel/traverse). Verified on own lib/: 95 files, 0 parse failures, 1048 symbols, 3199 edges.","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-23T02:28:46.848Z"}
